---
import { plan } from "../lib/plans";
const free = plan("free_v1");
const enterprise = plan("enterprise_v1");
---

<h2 class="text-fg" id="subprocessors">Service providers and storage</h2>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  Gateway compute and the primary trace and account databases are in Germany. This is not an EU-only processing
  promise: the service also uses global edge services, a secondary backup outside the EU-jurisdiction bucket, and
  identity, payment and email providers whose processing locations are provider-managed.
  Customer-selectable region pinning is not offered.
</p>
<dl class="text-fg-muted">
  <dt class="mt-5 font-semibold text-fg">Hetzner</dt>
  <dd>Gateway and ingest compute, messaging, and ClickHouse hot storage. Falkenstein, Germany.</dd>
  <dt class="mt-5 font-semibold text-fg">Cloudflare</dt>
  <dd>CDN and Workers for the website and dashboard; D1 for the website updates list;
    R2 for cold trace storage and backup archives. Edge and website processing is
    global; cold storage and primary backups use the EU jurisdiction. The secondary
    backup uses Cloudflare's default jurisdiction, without an EU-only restriction.</dd>
  <dt class="mt-5 font-semibold text-fg">Neon</dt>
  <dd>Postgres for accounts, workspace settings, encrypted provider credentials,
    billing metadata, and the canonical audit ledger. Frankfurt, Germany.</dd>
  <dt class="mt-5 font-semibold text-fg">WorkOS</dt>
  <dd>Authentication, users, organizations and workspace membership. Provider-managed locations.</dd>
  <dt class="mt-5 font-semibold text-fg">Polar</dt>
  <dd>Subscriptions, payment processing and invoicing. Provider-managed locations.</dd>
  <dt class="mt-5 font-semibold text-fg">Resend</dt>
  <dd>Transactional billing and usage emails when email delivery is configured:
    recipient address and notification content. Provider-managed locations.</dd>
</dl>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  Model providers receive requests selected by your application using your own
  provider credentials. Their retention and deletion policies apply to those requests.
  Audit anchoring also uses the public Sigstore Rekor transparency log for hashes,
  rather than trace payloads. See the
  <a href="https://docs.tracelane.dev/security" class="link-accent">security documentation</a>
  for that boundary.
</p>

<h2 class="text-fg" id="retention">Retention</h2>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  Captured traffic has a plan-defined queryable history: {free.queryable_days} days
  on Free and {enterprise.queryable_days} days on paid plans. The indexed window
  controls the recent range used for fast queries; it is not the deletion window.
  The retention sweep removes traffic older than the workspace's effective
  queryable window. Curated datasets and experiments are outside that traffic sweep.
  See <a href="/pricing" class="link-accent">pricing</a> for the plan windows.
</p>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  Audit ledger records and their verification anchors are retained separately,
  including after workspace deletion. Deleting a workspace does not remove its
  history from the tamper-evident ledger.
</p>

<h2 class="text-fg" id="deletion">Workspace deletion and recovery</h2>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  An owner can delete a workspace in Settings by confirming its name. This archives
  the workspace and marks its API keys revoked; access checks take effect as
  authorization caches refresh. Contact support during the 30-day recovery window
  if the deletion was accidental. The purge job selects workspaces archived for
  more than 30 days. Failed purges need operator review and deletion-status
  confirmation; this is not an
  immediate wipe or a guarantee that every copy disappears on day 30.
</p>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  The purge removes classified tenant data from the online telemetry and account
  stores, including stored provider-key rows, while retaining ledger records and
  anchors. It checks the target rows and other tenants' row counts. An unclassified
  tenant table stops the purge for review. Identity-provider deletion and subscription
  cancellation are best-effort steps and need separate confirmation if they fail.
</p>
<p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
  Shared backup archives are not rewritten for each workspace deletion; backup
  pruning and storage lifecycle rules are separate from the workspace purge.
  Vendor-held billing records and data already sent to your model providers have
  their own retention rules. For a deletion-status confirmation, a personal-data
  request, or removal from the website updates list, contact
  <a href="mailto:support@tracelane.dev" class="link-accent">support@tracelane.dev</a>.
</p>
